        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c62dadcd-4595-5305-9cdc-0a0ca1accc96",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: The Country Bears, The Wild\n- People: Peter Hastings, Steve \"Spaz\" Williams, Ed Decter, John J. Strauss, Mark Gibson, Philip Halprin, Candy Ford\n- Companies: Walt Disney Pictures, NBC\n- Attractions: Country Bear Jamboree\n- Television Programs: The Rerun Show, Curb Your Enthusiasm, Will & Grace, Girls Behaving Badly\n- Games: Law & Order videogame\n\nFacts:\n- Candy Ford was born on May 1, 1975.\n- The Country Bears is a 2002 American family musical comedy film directed by Peter Hastings, produced by Walt Disney Pictures, and based on the Disney theme park attraction Country Bear Jamboree.\n- Candy Ford voiced Trixie in the 2002 film The Country Bears.\n- Candy Ford is an American comedian and television actress best known for starring in the sketch comedy program The Rerun Show.\n- Candy Ford also appeared in Curb Your Enthusiasm and Will & Grace, provided voice work for the Law & Order videogame, and later starred in Girls Behaving Badly.\n- The Wild is a 2006 American 3D computer-animated comedy film directed by Steve \"Spaz\" Williams and written by Ed Decter, John J. Strauss, Mark Gibson, and Philip Halprin.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "bc2703a3-0859-554b-931b-dbfebac77a67",
        "text": "Page: The Country Bears. Sentence: The Country Bears is a 2002 American family musical comedy film, directed by Peter Hastings, produced by Walt Disney Pictures, and based on the Disney theme park attraction \"Country Bear Jamboree\".\nPage: The Wild. Sentence: The Wild is a 2006 American 3D computer animated comedy directed by animator Steve \"Spaz\" Williams, and written by Ed Decter, John J. Strauss, Mark Gibson and Philip Halprin.\nPage: Candy Ford. Sentence: Candy Ford (born May 1, 1975) is an American comedian and television actress, best known for starring in the sketch comedy, \"The Rerun Show\", Ford has also appeared in other TV programs including: \"Curb Your Enthusiasm\", \"Will & Grace\", and she provided voicework for the \"Law & Order\" videogame, and starred on the short-lived NBC sketch comedy, \"The Rerun Show\" and voiced Trixie in the film \"The Country Bears\" and later starred in \"Girls Behaving Badly\".",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
